WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:03.063
Tom is here for another day

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.570
This one's a little heavy.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.673
Cables to the workshop

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.278
Where you wanna go?

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.380
lets move it down there

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.784
We will use two

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.487
Because you can fill up another when i’m dumping

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.589
Yeah.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.792
I need to get that square faced shovel

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.762
That's the best one, I think. Yeah,

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.930
it's a bit flatter.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.765
Yeah.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.943
so a bit more gravel there...

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.013
I'll put some butter on it
and toast it in the pan.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:10.316
Sounds good.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.535
Is the bread dry?

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.938
a little bit, yea

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.940
the trick is a little sprinkle of water.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:34.707
and then toast it

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.710
it will steam it from the inside.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.948
that's how they do it at the bakery as well.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.816
If they didn't sell
the bread from yesterday.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.287
And the oven has a steamer

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:51.357
Put it in a hot oven with hot steam, and it will revitalize it

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.360
nice.

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:14.634
That's ok

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:18.771
That's not.

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:40.760
I can’t put in gravel
with the drainpipe there, no?

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:42.128
I have to wait.

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:44.530
I have to glue these ones up. Okay.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.865
It's a different system.

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:48.768
 leftovers from...

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:51.771
From another job? Yeah.

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:55.274
So, yeah, I can go on top of the burrito

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:04.050
the solid pipes will be connected to the rain gutters

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:37.236
3G10/7AWG underground cable

00:13:51.564 --> 00:13:54.400
the old trailer is repaired

00:16:51.143 --> 00:16:58.117
fertilized eggs from a local chicken breed: Millefiori Piemontese

00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:51.048
Enough digging for this week.

00:35:51.048 --> 00:35:53.718
Quite a lot of soil has moved

00:35:53.718 --> 00:35:56.721
out of the trench and back into it.

00:35:59.123 --> 00:36:01.592
Yeah, the drainpipes are all in

00:36:01.592 --> 00:36:04.562
that we dug yesterday or last week.

00:36:04.629 --> 00:36:07.265
So there’s two pipes on either side.

00:36:07.265 --> 00:36:08.900
One for the roof drainage.

00:36:08.900 --> 00:36:10.968
So later I'll connect rain gutters.

00:36:12.603 --> 00:36:15.907
And the other pipe is a perforated French drain

00:36:16.674 --> 00:36:18.910
for ground water
that comes near the cabin.

00:36:18.910 --> 00:36:21.212
So they can both separately drain.

00:36:21.212 --> 00:36:27.485
I could have connected them half way,
but it's kind of nice to see if I can see them dripping.

00:36:29.587 --> 00:36:34.892
Later, they will be connected with the drainage of the second cabin, which will be dug

00:36:34.892 --> 00:36:37.695
probably next year.

00:36:37.695 --> 00:36:42.934
And then there's also a water pipe going in, for a faucet

00:36:42.934 --> 00:36:45.636
and, drainage coming out.

00:36:45.636 --> 00:36:51.075
the channels for that were already built in underneath foundation before we poured it.

00:36:51.776 --> 00:36:54.779
Two years ago. And,

00:36:55.413 --> 00:36:58.282
Yeah, that drain was sitting quite deep.

00:36:58.282 --> 00:37:00.785
And because it needs to slope down,

00:37:00.785 --> 00:37:05.890
I needed to dig a very deep trench there just in front of the door.

00:37:06.257 --> 00:37:09.126
That's all in there
now, as well as electricity cables.

00:37:11.629 --> 00:37:17.969
Two, because I need to run the machine simultaneously,
like a dust extractor and a saw.

00:37:18.002 --> 00:37:21.272
So they're on two separate groups,
quite thick cables.

00:37:21.472 --> 00:37:24.208
10mm2

00:37:24.208 --> 00:37:27.979
I think in gauge, that’s 8 eight gauge

00:37:30.681 --> 00:37:33.317
They need to be six because otherwise
it could be a voltage drop

00:37:33.317 --> 00:37:36.921
because some machines
that will draw 3kW or so.

00:37:38.856 --> 00:37:39.190
Yeah.

00:37:39.190 --> 00:37:41.692
So that's all in there.

00:37:41.692 --> 00:37:44.695
And, yea it was quite a rainy week.

00:37:45.263 --> 00:37:47.665
Beautiful today.

00:37:47.665 --> 00:37:50.101
a little bit more digging to do.

00:37:50.101 --> 00:37:52.770
to fill the trench on the other side.

00:37:52.770 --> 00:37:55.706
I think another a load of gravel,

00:37:55.706 --> 00:37:57.575
and then we're getting there.

00:37:57.575 --> 00:37:59.310
Clean it up,

00:37:59.310 --> 00:38:01.412
seed some grass,

00:38:01.412 --> 00:38:06.150
put some gravel on the roads,
and then it looks like, neat again.

